## 2. Log Implementation

### Development (Local)
```javascript
// Use console methods with structured data
console.info('[DONATION] Order created', { order_id, amount });
console.error('[WEBHOOK] Signature verification failed', { ip, event_type });
console.warn('[AUTH] Failed login attempt', { email, ip });
```

### Production (Vercel)
- Vercel automatically captures `console.log` output
- View logs: Vercel Dashboard → Project → Logs
- Filter by: Function name, level, time range
- Retention: 1 hour (Free), 3 days (Pro)

### Structured Logging Format
```javascript
// Helper function for consistent logging
function log(level, category, message, data = {}) {
  const entry = {
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    level,
    category,
    message,
    ...data
  };
  
  switch (level) {
    case 'ERROR': console.error(JSON.stringify(entry)); break;
    case 'WARN':  console.warn(JSON.stringify(entry)); break;
    case 'INFO':  console.info(JSON.stringify(entry)); break;
    case 'DEBUG': console.debug(JSON.stringify(entry)); break;
  }
}

// Usage
log('INFO', 'DONATION', 'Order created', { order_id: 'order_xxx', amount: 500 });
log('ERROR', 'WEBHOOK', 'Signature invalid', { ip: '1.2.3.4' });
```

